Third-party notices
-------------------

Each dependency below is used unmodified and installed from its public
registry; none of its source is vendored into this repository (the one
vendored third-party file is described next). The licence
of every npm and Python dependency is checked by gate:licenses, with the
weak-copyleft exceptions recorded in license-exceptions.json. On the npm
side that is the pnpm workspace and every project that installs from its
own package-lock.json (the terminal's images run `npm ci` from one). The
retiring dashboard (services/dashboard) and the transcript-rendering copy
it vendors are outside the gates, and this line builds neither. Binaries
and model weights built into the images are listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

One file is vendored and modified:
core/runtime/src/runtime_kernel/seccomp-userns.json is derived from the
default seccomp profile of the Moby project
(https://github.com/moby/profiles, seccomp/default.json, as vendored in
Docker Engine 29.6.2), Copyright Docker, Inc. and the Moby project
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Vexa added one
rule (allowing user namespaces for meeting bots' browser sandbox); the file
says so. Its licence text is licenses/moby-profiles.LICENSE.txt, and travels
beside it as seccomp-userns.LICENSE.txt.

